# Gryphon Forge — Cursor Rules

## Project Context

gryphon-forge deploys Red Hat OpenShift (OCP) via User-Provisioned Infrastructure (UPI) using Ansible. It consumes gryphon-foundry outputs and transitions from an empty VPC to a functional cluster.

## Ansible Conventions

- Use FQCN for modules (e.g., `ansible.builtin.copy`, not `copy`).
- All roles must be idempotent; tasks should be safe to run multiple times.
- Use `ansible-lint` before committing; fix reported issues.
- Run validation commands before committing (see AGENTS.md "Validation & Testing").
- Prefer `include_vars` and `set_fact` for configuration; keep secrets out of playbooks.
- Use `tags` on tasks for targeted runs (ignition, ec2, csr_approval, validation).

## File Layout

- `inventory/group_vars/all.yml` — Main config (foundry outputs, cluster metadata, node counts).
- `roles/<name>/` — Each role has `tasks/main.yml`, `defaults/main.yml`, and `README.md`.
- Playbooks live in `playbooks/`; main entry is `deploy_cluster.yml`.

## Key Variables

- `foundry_*` — From gryphon-foundry (vpc_id, private_subnets, bastion_sg, hosted_zone, region).
- `cluster_name`, `base_domain`, `ocp_version` — Cluster identity (`ocp_cluster_name` / `ocp_base_domain` from foundry override these when set).
- `*_count`, `*_instance_type` — Node sizing (master, worker, gpu_worker).
- `install_dir`, `foundry_output_path`, `pull_secret_path`, `ssh_public_key_path`.

## Immutable Infrastructure

OCP nodes (RHCOS) are immutable. Do not add Ansible tasks that modify node OS directly. Use MachineConfigs or cluster operators for node-level changes.

## AWS & OpenShift

- EC2 provisioning uses `amazon.aws` and `community.aws` collections.
- Ignition generation uses `openshift-install` from `install_dir/bin/` (auto-downloaded from `forge_ocp_mirror_*`, same channel as bastion) or `openshift_install_binary_path` when set.
- Route53 records use `foundry_internal_hosted_zone_id` for internal DNS.

## When Editing

- Adding roles: Create `roles/<name>/` with tasks, defaults, and README.
- Changing config: Prefer `inventory/group_vars/all.yml` or role `defaults/main.yml`.
- New playbook tags: Add to the role block in `deploy_cluster.yml`.
- New playbooks: Add them to the syntax-check step in `.github/workflows/ansible-validation.yml`.
- Validation changes: Run `ansible-playbook <playbook> --syntax-check` and `ansible-lint` locally; update workflow or `.ansible-lint` if validation logic changes.
